{%- comment -%}
  schema-page-article — Article structured data for a guide or education page.

  Added 23/09/2026 (W333). The Searchable AI-visibility audit rated the
  education pages High for "no author", "no publication or last-updated
  date" and "Article schema is missing": they emitted JewelryStore, WebSite,
  BreadcrumbList and FAQPage, but nothing saying who wrote them or when.
  Answer engines weigh exactly that when choosing a source.

  RENDERED FROM layout/theme.liquid, in <head>, only when the page carries the
  fye.updated_on date metafield (the 53 guide and chapter pages):

      {% render 'schema-page-article', page: page %}

  dateModified is that metafield, the same date the visible author line in
  heading-template prints, so the two cannot drift. datePublished is the
  page's own publish date. The publisher is the JewelryStore by @id.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if page != blank and page.metafields.fye.updated_on != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign updated = page.metafields.fye.updated_on.value | default: page.metafields.fye.updated_on
    assign published = page.published_at | default: updated
  -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "@id": {{ canonical_url | append: '#article' | json }},
  "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": {{ canonical_url | json }} },
  "headline": {{ page.title | strip_html | truncate: 110 | json }},
  {%- if page_description != blank %}
  "description": {{ page_description | strip_html | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  "datePublished": {{ published | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | json }},
  "dateModified": {{ updated | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | json }},
  "author": {% render 'schema-person', name: 'Edward Marno' %},
  "publisher": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#business' | json }} },
  "inLanguage": "en-GB",
  "isAccessibleForFree": true
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
